{"assets":["/statement-assets/27c925ed02ee7c3e6737742d26f9cb7f5fcb7923d26e8caa254cf26faa91fbe6.png","/statement-assets/67b12c4072b290538d5a100b4d8e284194e5420851e573b9ccda0e61d3535a4f.png","/statement-assets/ae0f5938e091c709011d37d7e4e7045a8a5476b6db767dbf8aba07451d674262.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1325","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Ehab's Last Theorem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's the year 5555. You have a graph, and you want to find a long cycle and a huge independent set, just because you can. But for now, let's just stick with finding either."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given a connected graph with $$$n$$$ vertices, you can choose to either:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" find an independent set that has "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\lceil\\sqrt{n}\\rceil$$$ vertices."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" find a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"simple"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" cycle of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at least"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\lceil\\sqrt{n}\\rceil$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An independent set is a set of vertices such that no two of them are connected by an edge. A simple cycle is a cycle that doesn't contain any vertex twice. I have a proof you can always solve one of these problems, but it's too long to fit this margin."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$5 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$, $$$n-1 \\le m \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of vertices and edges in the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$m$$$ lines contains two space-separated integers $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$ ($$$1 \\le u,v \\le n$$$) that mean there's an edge between vertices $$$u$$$ and $$$v$$$. It's guaranteed that the graph is connected and doesn't contain any self-loops or multiple edges."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you choose to solve the first problem, then on the first line print \"1\", followed by a line containing $$$\\lceil\\sqrt{n}\\rceil$$$ distinct integers not exceeding $$$n$$$, the vertices in the desired independent set."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you, however, choose to solve the second problem, then on the first line print \"2\", followed by a line containing one integer, $$$c$$$, representing the length of the found cycle, followed by a line containing $$$c$$$ distinct integers integers not exceeding $$$n$$$, the vertices in the desired cycle, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in the order they appear in the cycle"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 6\n1 3\n3 4\n4 2\n2 6\n5 6\n5 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n1 6 4"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6 8\n1 3\n3 4\n4 2\n2 6\n5 6\n5 1\n1 4\n2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4\n1 5 2 4"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5 4\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n3 4 5 "}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/27c925ed02ee7c3e6737742d26f9cb7f5fcb7923d26e8caa254cf26faa91fbe6.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Notice that you can solve either problem, so printing the cycle $$$2-4-3-1-5-6$$$ is also acceptable."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/67b12c4072b290538d5a100b4d8e284194e5420851e573b9ccda0e61d3535a4f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Notice that if there are multiple answers you can print any, so printing the cycle $$$2-5-6$$$, for example, is acceptable."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ae0f5938e091c709011d37d7e4e7045a8a5476b6db767dbf8aba07451d674262.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1325F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1325/problem/F"}